WEBVTT

00:01:31.220 --> 00:01:34.760
Are you also here to help 
with the reconstruction? 

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:36.360
Well, something like that. 

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:42.330
The city needs a lot of workers to help 
with the rebuilding and construction. 

00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:46.620
Would you like to go out somewhere 
together on Sunday, Joey?

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:47.700
Yeah!

00:01:49.630 --> 00:01:52.050
I was asked out on a date!

00:01:52.050 --> 00:01:54.110
What do you think, Heroman?

00:01:54.110 --> 00:01:57.380
I wonder where Lina would enjoy going to?

00:02:01.540 --> 00:02:03.240
Now, time for work.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:51.920
Joey...

00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:54.900
Hey, Joey!

00:02:56.360 --> 00:02:58.280
What's the matter, Joey?

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:00.530
S-Sorry...

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:04.950
Worried about something?

00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:07.830
N-No, I'm not...

00:03:08.970 --> 00:03:10.030
I see.

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:14.960
Um, Mister...

00:03:15.450 --> 00:03:16.670
Suppose you were...

00:03:16.670 --> 00:03:21.230
Come on Joey, stop calling 
me "Mister" already...

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:24.170
My name is Axel Hughes.

00:03:24.530 --> 00:03:25.300
Pleased to meet you.

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:26.580
Sure!

00:03:29.080 --> 00:03:32.220
So, what was it you wanted to ask me about?

00:03:34.610 --> 00:03:36.680
You see, tomorrow...

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:38.690
A date?

00:03:39.320 --> 00:03:41.530
You and me going on a date?

00:03:41.530 --> 00:03:43.380
No, duh...

00:03:43.380 --> 00:03:45.350
I'm talking about Joey.

00:03:45.350 --> 00:03:46.850
You're going on a date with Joey?

00:03:46.850 --> 00:03:48.500
Joey and <i>Lina</i>!

00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:50.850
Oh, those two.

00:03:55.730 --> 00:03:57.750
Are you serious about that?!

00:03:57.750 --> 00:04:00.670
I've told you like, how many times already?

00:04:28.900 --> 00:04:29.940
Lina!

00:04:30.410 --> 00:04:32.010
Sorry!

00:04:32.010 --> 00:04:32.870
Were you waiting?

00:04:33.150 --> 00:04:36.330
No! I just got here myself!

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:40.370
What is she talking about? She's 
been waiting for 30 minutes!

00:04:40.370 --> 00:04:45.090
Um, Psy... Don't you think this 
is an invasion of their privacy?

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:47.300
Nothing of the sort.

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:49.020
This is friendship!

00:04:49.020 --> 00:04:52.790
I'm looking out for him, and 
there's nothing wrong with that.

00:04:52.790 --> 00:04:55.380
It looks like we're totally stalkers!

00:04:55.380 --> 00:04:57.580
Don't yell in my ear like that!

00:04:57.580 --> 00:05:00.280
This is the first date Joey's 
ever had in his life.

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:04.380
If we can't help support him at 
a time like this, when can we?

00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:06.220
The first?

00:05:06.820 --> 00:05:11.720
Joey there'll screw up the second 
we leave him alone, I know it!

00:05:11.720 --> 00:05:16.910
I don't want to spend my precious 
weekend doing this sort of thing either!

00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:20.650
There goes a day's worth of pay from my job.

00:05:20.650 --> 00:05:23.050
You look like you're 
enjoying yourself plenty.

00:05:23.050 --> 00:05:24.960
You're no fun.

00:05:25.590 --> 00:05:27.290
Looks like they're on the move.

00:05:28.820 --> 00:05:31.270
Where do they plan to go, I wonder?

00:05:31.850 --> 00:05:33.640
I'm heading off!

00:05:33.640 --> 00:05:35.850
Do your best not to be discovered!

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:41.930
Crap!

00:05:41.930 --> 00:05:43.280
Something the matter?

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:44.280
Hey!

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:46.320
Hold it!

00:05:48.040 --> 00:05:49.560
Oh, Psy.

00:05:49.560 --> 00:05:51.410
What are you doing here?

00:05:51.410 --> 00:05:53.670
That's what I should be asking!

00:05:54.890 --> 00:05:56.790
Why are <i>you</i> here, Holly?

00:05:57.770 --> 00:05:58.880
'Cause...

00:06:00.190 --> 00:06:03.880
Joey's been acting strange 
ever since yesterday.

00:06:04.890 --> 00:06:07.990
He was fussing with his hair in 
front of the mirror this morning.

00:06:07.990 --> 00:06:10.680
Brushed his teeth super carefully...

00:06:11.450 --> 00:06:15.060
Then snuck out of the house 
trying not to be seen.

00:06:18.310 --> 00:06:21.620
So I thought: "This has <i>got</i> to be a date!"

00:06:21.620 --> 00:06:23.270
I, as his big sister, came to heckle him!

00:06:23.270 --> 00:06:25.690
I'm begging you, don't!

00:06:25.690 --> 00:06:26.780
Why?

00:06:27.640 --> 00:06:31.350
If you join in it won't be a date anymore!

00:06:31.350 --> 00:06:34.760
Fine, fine. Then I'll call 
it somethin' different.

00:06:34.760 --> 00:06:36.590
I, as his big sister...

00:06:37.160 --> 00:06:38.590
...will blow his date to smithereens!

00:06:38.590 --> 00:06:40.270
That's even worse!

00:06:40.270 --> 00:06:41.670
You got a problem with that?

00:06:41.670 --> 00:06:45.050
Pardon the interruption, you two.

00:06:45.050 --> 00:06:45.770
Who are you?

00:06:45.770 --> 00:06:48.080
Let's save the fighting for later.

00:06:48.080 --> 00:06:50.630
We're going to lose track of 
Joey and Lina at this rate.

00:06:51.600 --> 00:06:53.180
They're heading to the next place!

00:06:53.180 --> 00:06:56.100
That direction is probably...

00:07:09.490 --> 00:07:12.330
It's been so long since 
I've been to the ocean!

00:07:12.980 --> 00:07:14.160
Hey, Joey!

00:07:16.800 --> 00:07:17.990
Let's swim!

00:07:17.990 --> 00:07:20.480
Yahoo!

00:07:31.860 --> 00:07:35.560
I can't believe I'm able to spend 
a day together with Lina like this!

00:07:36.280 --> 00:07:38.430
What's the matter, Joey?

00:07:38.430 --> 00:07:41.230
Hurry up! Hurry up!

00:07:41.230 --> 00:07:43.600
S-Sure, I'm coming!

00:07:45.760 --> 00:07:48.250
So, who's the broad?

00:07:48.250 --> 00:07:51.990
Lina. She's a cheerleader 
in the same grade as Joey.

00:07:51.990 --> 00:07:54.410
A stuck-up rich girl?

00:07:54.410 --> 00:07:57.540
That don't match no matter 
how you look at it.

00:07:57.540 --> 00:08:01.330
And that's why we're helping him, got it?

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:03.750
Fine. And who're you, old dude?

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:04.870
Old dude?

00:08:04.870 --> 00:08:07.110
That's Prof. Denton.

00:08:07.110 --> 00:08:09.020
He's the science teacher at our school.

00:08:09.020 --> 00:08:12.050
A lot of stuff happened, 
and we're all pals now.

00:08:13.250 --> 00:08:15.030
Man, have you guys lost it.

00:08:15.030 --> 00:08:16.970
You're friends with a teacher?

00:08:16.970 --> 00:08:20.380
And who is this girl who doesn't mince words?

00:08:20.380 --> 00:08:24.810
She's Holly, Joey's sister. 
She was born rude.

00:08:24.810 --> 00:08:27.900
Yup, that's basically it. Nice to meetcha.

00:08:28.940 --> 00:08:30.070
And you, as well.

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:41.200
Hey! Stop it Joey!

00:08:41.200 --> 00:08:44.850
The more you say you don't like 
it, the more you want it, right?

00:08:44.850 --> 00:08:46.710
Oh, now you've gone too far!

00:08:47.060 --> 00:08:48.710
Lina's counterattack!

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:51.630
Don't count me out yet...

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:54.400
Are you two having fun?

00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:55.820
It's boring!

00:08:56.370 --> 00:08:59.550
Everything's actually going 
pretty smoothly for those two.

00:08:59.550 --> 00:09:01.510
So I guess we aren't needed?

00:09:01.510 --> 00:09:04.090
That's a good thing, right?

00:09:04.090 --> 00:09:05.770
Professor Denton?

00:09:07.230 --> 00:09:08.810
Ms. Collins!

00:09:09.260 --> 00:09:11.220
What in the world are you doing?

00:09:11.220 --> 00:09:12.310
We're stalking.

00:09:20.050 --> 00:09:22.140
Joey and Lina?

00:09:22.610 --> 00:09:26.840
So isn't this... an invasion of privacy?

00:09:26.840 --> 00:09:29.430
What's wrong with a big sister 
worrying about her little brother?

00:09:29.430 --> 00:09:32.280
What's wrong with his 
friend worrying about him?

00:09:32.280 --> 00:09:35.800
For me, although I am a teacher, I 
don't think I'm doing anything...

00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:38.290
Even so, you shouldn't be doing this!

00:09:40.330 --> 00:09:41.690
They're on the move?

00:09:43.720 --> 00:09:47.960
Where? Where? I can't see 
Joey and Lina anywhere!

00:09:53.120 --> 00:09:56.230
P-Pardon me...

00:09:59.480 --> 00:10:02.250
Should we really be doing this?

00:10:03.330 --> 00:10:06.040
That's... They're planning on getting lunch?

00:10:10.970 --> 00:10:13.830
I can't... I can't!

00:10:13.830 --> 00:10:16.170
They're really heading to that restaurant.

00:10:18.850 --> 00:10:22.010
This is bad! This is real bad!

00:10:41.830 --> 00:10:44.210
And what's so bad about this?

00:10:44.210 --> 00:10:47.490
Joey has never been to such 
a high-class restaurant!

00:10:47.490 --> 00:10:50.700
On the other hand, Lina's filthy rich!

00:10:50.700 --> 00:10:55.960
Joey's going to be red-faced embarrassed 
when he's not able to order anything!

00:10:55.960 --> 00:10:57.730
So, let 'im be.

00:10:57.730 --> 00:10:59.130
They're no match for each other anyway.

00:10:59.430 --> 00:11:01.800
I can't! I can't!

00:11:01.800 --> 00:11:03.180
Don't worry.

00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:06.080
I thought something like this would 
happen, so I gave him some advice.

00:11:06.080 --> 00:11:07.130
What?

00:11:07.130 --> 00:11:09.230
Don't enter any expensive 
looking restaurants.

00:11:12.310 --> 00:11:14.060
They just entered!

00:11:14.400 --> 00:11:16.120
Well, that's odd.

00:11:16.120 --> 00:11:18.160
We've got to do something!

00:11:18.160 --> 00:11:19.940
At this rate, Joey will...

00:11:19.940 --> 00:11:22.550
I can't!

00:11:27.750 --> 00:11:30.080
This restaurant is quite good.

00:11:32.100 --> 00:11:33.750
What'll you have, Joey?

00:11:36.100 --> 00:11:38.500
Oh, what a coincidence, you two!

00:11:38.500 --> 00:11:43.210
I was out for a jog, and I 
just happened to run into you!

00:11:43.210 --> 00:11:44.510
Ms. Collins!

00:11:44.510 --> 00:11:47.050
A-At this restaurant...

00:11:47.050 --> 00:11:49.220
I recommend the caviar 
salad and clam chowder,

00:11:49.220 --> 00:11:53.600
the lobster for the main course, 
and the panna cotta for dessert!

00:12:06.450 --> 00:12:07.990
Raw oysters are good, right?

00:12:07.990 --> 00:12:09.280
Yeah!

00:12:09.280 --> 00:12:12.780
I'm really glad you ordered 
all that stuff for me, Lina.

00:12:12.780 --> 00:12:16.310
Next time we'll try what 
Ms. Collins recommended.

00:12:17.950 --> 00:12:19.380
I knew it, they're here.

00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:21.630
Sounds good, right?

00:12:22.120 --> 00:12:23.660
O-Of course!

00:13:09.510 --> 00:13:10.510
Lina.

00:13:10.510 --> 00:13:12.010
Y-Yes?

00:13:12.520 --> 00:13:13.520
Let's run!

00:13:15.360 --> 00:13:16.370
He noticed us?

00:13:16.370 --> 00:13:17.230
You won't get away!

00:13:17.550 --> 00:13:19.230
J-Joey, what's the matter?

00:13:19.230 --> 00:13:20.330
This way!

00:13:20.730 --> 00:13:21.980
Ladies second!

00:13:23.480 --> 00:13:25.930
I can't! I can't!

00:13:25.930 --> 00:13:27.800
Then don't come with us!

00:13:27.800 --> 00:13:30.570
I can't! I can't do that!

00:13:33.740 --> 00:13:34.660
Ladies first!

00:13:45.690 --> 00:13:47.080
Miss Jones!

00:13:48.260 --> 00:13:49.230
Where's Joey?

00:13:52.070 --> 00:13:53.260
Where's Joey?

00:13:53.870 --> 00:13:55.680
I lost 'im.

00:13:55.680 --> 00:13:59.230
The little sucker's always 
been fast at runnin' away.

00:14:04.140 --> 00:14:05.910
We should be fine outside.

00:14:05.910 --> 00:14:07.400
Fine from what?

00:14:08.530 --> 00:14:12.030
Why'd you suddenly start running?

00:14:12.030 --> 00:14:13.940
S-Sorry.

00:14:13.940 --> 00:14:15.040
How should I put this...

00:14:16.320 --> 00:14:17.400
I'm really sorry!

00:14:17.400 --> 00:14:18.870
In exchange...

00:14:17.640 --> 00:14:21.250
<i>We have breaking news to report.</i>

00:14:21.660 --> 00:14:27.380
<i>It looks like a robot used in the 
reconstruction has gone out of control.</i>

00:14:27.380 --> 00:14:29.820
<i>This is Keisha, reporting.</i>

00:14:29.820 --> 00:14:34.760
<i>Generas Industries' robot, MR-1, is moving 
out from the center of Center city...</i>

00:14:35.470 --> 00:14:37.430
<i>Get the shot!</i>

00:14:39.640 --> 00:14:40.690
<i>According to reports...</i>

00:14:40.690 --> 00:14:43.450
Oh no, it's heading this way!

00:14:44.240 --> 00:14:47.270
I guess that's it for our 
date then. Too bad...

00:14:48.620 --> 00:14:51.010
You're going, right?

00:14:52.140 --> 00:14:53.360
Wait, I mean...

00:14:53.780 --> 00:14:54.870
Go!

00:14:54.870 --> 00:14:56.410
You're a hero, Joey!

00:14:58.040 --> 00:14:58.900
Right.

00:14:59.200 --> 00:15:02.500
It's okay! Don't worry about me.

00:15:02.500 --> 00:15:03.750
I already had plenty of fun today.

00:15:04.090 --> 00:15:05.920
When I get back, let's 
go to the amusement park!

00:15:06.250 --> 00:15:07.960
Huh? The amusement park?

00:15:08.660 --> 00:15:12.220
I'll be back, for sure. 
So, will you wait for me?

00:15:15.950 --> 00:15:19.060
Got it. Can we ride the 
ferris wheel together later?

00:15:19.060 --> 00:15:19.950
Sure.

00:15:20.970 --> 00:15:22.140
Go get 'em.

00:15:23.340 --> 00:15:24.560
I'm off.

00:15:24.560 --> 00:15:25.890
Be careful.

00:15:25.890 --> 00:15:26.820
I will!

00:15:35.180 --> 00:15:36.830
Are you sure about this?

00:15:36.830 --> 00:15:39.090
Pretending like it's gone out of control?

00:15:39.090 --> 00:15:41.260
Our company's reputation is sunk.

00:15:41.260 --> 00:15:44.670
Reputation? Have you 
people forgotten already?

00:15:44.670 --> 00:15:47.990
The plan for the MR-1 going 
out of control came from

00:15:47.990 --> 00:15:51.590
the agency above the military 
directly connected to the President,

00:15:52.180 --> 00:15:54.840
the NIA!

00:15:55.190 --> 00:15:59.190
Oh, so you actually 
accepted that nutty offer?

00:15:59.190 --> 00:16:03.810
They wanted us to lure out the Ghost and 
to bust it up with the MR-1, right?

00:16:03.810 --> 00:16:05.790
Exactly!

00:16:05.790 --> 00:16:09.520
The time for our revenge is near!

00:16:09.520 --> 00:16:13.360
We can prove that we have the ultimate weapon

00:16:13.360 --> 00:16:16.930
to all of North America if we 
are able to defeat the Ghost.

00:16:16.930 --> 00:16:18.970
If we get it formally 
adopted by the military,

00:16:18.970 --> 00:16:21.540
it's only a matter of time until 
it's introduced to the entire world.

00:16:21.820 --> 00:16:24.360
What are you guys doing standing around?

00:16:24.360 --> 00:16:26.030
Keep your eyes peeled!

00:16:26.030 --> 00:16:27.250
Yes, sir!

00:16:30.880 --> 00:16:32.190
Is that it?

00:16:36.670 --> 00:16:38.920
I have to hurry before 
it crashes into the city.

00:16:43.150 --> 00:16:44.870
That guy might appear again.

00:16:49.480 --> 00:16:52.190
Anyway, I have to stop that robot now!

00:16:58.070 --> 00:17:01.030
Heroman... Engage!

00:17:20.810 --> 00:17:24.310
There you are, Ghost!

00:17:24.310 --> 00:17:27.980
I've wanted to meet you, you bastard!

00:17:27.980 --> 00:17:32.730
Now will be a moment that 
goes down in history!

00:17:34.310 --> 00:17:36.210
Make sure to take all the data you can.

00:17:36.210 --> 00:17:38.220
Don't miss even a second!

00:17:38.220 --> 00:17:39.930
I know, I know!

00:17:47.000 --> 00:17:48.000
Heroman!

00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:49.900
Think you can escape?

00:17:54.660 --> 00:17:55.830
This is strange.

00:17:56.240 --> 00:17:58.720
The news said that it went out of control,

00:17:58.720 --> 00:18:01.930
but that robot seems like it's 
being controlled by someone.

00:18:01.930 --> 00:18:03.930
I knew it. This is a trap!

00:18:05.780 --> 00:18:07.210
Is that all you got?

00:18:07.210 --> 00:18:09.320
Is that all you got, eh?

00:18:20.950 --> 00:18:23.620
What's that white thing?

00:18:26.310 --> 00:18:28.230
This is a scoop!

00:18:29.700 --> 00:18:31.120
That helicopter is...

00:18:31.120 --> 00:18:34.030
Did they see Heroman, I wonder?

00:18:34.030 --> 00:18:35.500
I've got to finish this up quick.

00:18:59.320 --> 00:19:00.030
The jaw?

00:19:00.030 --> 00:19:02.030
Heroman... Attack!

00:19:05.600 --> 00:19:07.370
He's tearing open the jaw!

00:19:15.500 --> 00:19:17.000
It's been overturned!

00:19:17.000 --> 00:19:19.200
I'm not done yet!

00:19:21.810 --> 00:19:24.270
You'll be in big trouble 
if you underestimate...

00:19:24.270 --> 00:19:27.180
...this pinnacle of my technology!

00:19:27.530 --> 00:19:28.730
Doctor!

00:19:31.940 --> 00:19:35.230
Heroman... Finish!

00:20:00.080 --> 00:20:02.690
Where'd that white thing go?

00:20:26.840 --> 00:20:27.700
Thanks for waiting!

00:20:28.530 --> 00:20:30.490
Is the city safe?

00:20:30.490 --> 00:20:32.960
Yeah! We stopped it, somehow.

00:20:32.960 --> 00:20:34.100
Good.

00:20:36.250 --> 00:20:38.770
It looks like it's closed already...

00:20:39.080 --> 00:20:40.280
Don't worry!

00:20:46.500 --> 00:20:48.430
Wow!

00:20:48.430 --> 00:20:52.680
I'm sorry. I wanted to actually ride 
inside the gondola for real...

00:20:52.680 --> 00:20:54.090
It's okay.

00:20:54.420 --> 00:20:57.710
You can't experience something 
like this every day, after all.

00:20:59.990 --> 00:21:01.270
This is...

00:21:26.390 --> 00:21:28.430
Thank you, Mr. Hughes.

00:21:29.180 --> 00:21:32.240
You shouldn't get hung up 
over making a date "go well."

00:21:32.240 --> 00:21:35.390
Don't think about that, just 
go with the flow, naturally.

00:21:40.050 --> 00:21:41.400
Oh, yeah...

00:21:41.750 --> 00:21:45.730
Girls love the night view. 
I'd say that much, at least.

00:21:47.150 --> 00:21:50.910
Thanks to Mr. Hughes, we 
had a successful date!

00:21:58.370 --> 00:21:59.710
That's...

00:22:01.800 --> 00:22:03.090
Agent Hughes.

00:22:03.960 --> 00:22:06.210
Did you find something?

00:22:06.210 --> 00:22:10.170
Yes. There's a boy with the Ghost.

00:22:14.210 --> 00:22:16.100
Joey Jones.

00:22:20.690 --> 00:22:24.090
<b>"Can you hear this voice?"</b>

00:22:24.090 --> 00:22:31.560
<b>I've been calling that, always, from deep within my heart.</b>

00:22:34.370 --> 00:22:45.460
<b>Would you, all alone, let another lonely one be next to you?</b>

00:22:45.460 --> 00:22:51.010
<b>Because together it's not lonely, it's twoly.</b>

00:22:51.010 --> 00:22:56.140
<b>See, you're not alone any longer.</b>

00:22:57.280 --> 00:22:59.990
<b>Just because there's no one next to me</b>

00:22:59.990 --> 00:23:02.540
<b>doesn't mean that I'm lonely!</b>

00:23:02.540 --> 00:23:07.740
<b>For someone to notice this pain</b>

00:23:07.740 --> 00:23:13.270
<b>that heart must have surely cried.</b>

00:23:13.270 --> 00:23:16.650
<b>Right now, we'll crush to bits</b>

00:23:16.650 --> 00:23:20.350
<b>the fortress of our limitless sadness!</b>

00:23:20.350 --> 00:23:24.050
<b>I'll take you with me!</b>

00:23:24.050 --> 00:23:27.730
<b>Got it? I'm running through at full power.</b>

00:23:27.730 --> 00:23:31.470
<b>To where you're waiting, left behind</b>

00:23:31.470 --> 00:23:34.640
<b>in the place of tears...</b>

00:23:35.950 --> 00:23:39.770
<b>I believe in you, with burning passion!</b>

00:23:39.770 --> 00:23:43.560
<b>Come to me!</b>

00:23:51.360 --> 00:23:53.400
On the next Heroman: 

00:23:53.710 --> 00:23:58.850
Everyone, farewell. I am leaving this city.

00:23:58.850 --> 00:24:01.660
With their identities revealed to the NIA, 

00:24:01.660 --> 00:24:05.210
Joey, Denton, as well as Psy all flee.

00:24:05.930 --> 00:24:08.420
Completely and utterly surrounded,

00:24:08.420 --> 00:24:11.600
can Joey and the others really slip through?

00:24:12.290 --> 00:24:15.990
Next time on Heroman #13: Getaway!

00:24:15.990 --> 00:24:19.210
Heroman... Attack!
